  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hydrogen reacts with carbon monoxide in presence of cobalt catalyst to give methanol.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mtext>Cobalt&#160;catalyst</mtext></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>As the mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is used for the synthesis of methanol and a number of hydrocarbons, it is called synthesis gas or <strong>syngas. </strong>The process of producing syngas&nbsp;from coal is called coal gasification.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mn>1270</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>The reaction of steam with hydrocarbons or coke at high temperature in presence of nickel catalyst gives a mixture of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, called water gas.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>1270</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></munderover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>Electrolysis of brine solution produces&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas at cathode and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas at anode.</p><p>Cathode:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Anode:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>The overall reaction is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So, the correct answer is A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I</p>"
  }
